  "reply_text": "Found one issue I’d fix before merging:\n\n**[P2] `topTags` mutates the input, breaking the sidebar’s recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`\n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array in place. `sidebar()` then reads that same array at `src/render.js:5`, so “recent” becomes the five highest-count tags rather than the first five tags supplied. This also violates the README’s non-mutation guarantee.\n\nReproduced with six tags: the original first tag disappears from “recent,” while the sixth tag moves into it because its count is higher. Sort a copy instead, and add regression tests verifying that `topTags` preserves its input and `sidebar().recent` preserves the supplied order.\n\n**Validation:** All 4 existing tests pass, but none checks input preservation or sidebar behavior. No files changed.",
